    {
        "content": "<p>hi all! i'm trying to help unblock <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/31898\">#31898</a> and could use some feedback. </p>\n<p>first, I opened <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39785\">#39785</a> which should let the antipode be written more naturally without <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/31898/changes#diff-36a09b8371f41a9ad0f901bb6a5f899e790aa88958478d44242ccaa76ff3f0c8R35-R52\">all these lemmas</a>. I'm feeling good about this part. </p>\n<p>then I was able to trim the <code>mul</code> case a bit (from ~100 to ~75 lines), but hit diminishing returns on the sweedler calculations, which seem like they're just kind of inherently a slog in mathlib right now? </p>\n<p>it occurred to me that we can use the fact that the elements of <code>A</code> where each antipode axiom hold form a subalgebra and construct <code>HopfAlgebra</code> by verifying on a small generating set. <del>in case this is potentially useful in other cases i made a PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39800\">#39800</a> which makes the <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/31898\">#31898</a> proof pretty compact:</del> (See below).</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instHopfAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HopfAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TensorAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofAlgHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">antipode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HopfAlgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mul_rTensor_comul_eq_of_adjoin_eq_top</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">adjoin_range_ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HopfAlgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mul_lTensor_comul_eq_of_adjoin_eq_top</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">adjoin_range_ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">rintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>longer-term, we'd obviously replace these with the more principled construction like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ofGradedConnected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">GradedConnectedBialgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HopfAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>but it seems like that's a ways off and perhaps the more ad hoc constructors are worth it?</p>",
        "id": 597455260,
        "sender_full_name": "Robert Hawkins",
        "timestamp": 1779676142
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Could you try defining <code>GradedConnectedBialgebra</code>, just to get an idea of how hard it is?</p>",
        "id": 597477448,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1779692085
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the definitions are not hard, I sketched something like this</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsGradedCoalgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">𝒜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DirectSum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Decomposition</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝒜</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">comul_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">},</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝒜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Coalgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"bp\">⨆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⨆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⨆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"n\">LinearMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TensorProduct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">𝒜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">subtype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">𝒜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">subtype</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConnected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">𝒜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">GradedAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝒜</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">zero_le_span_one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝒜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">span</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>so it's the \"existence of antipode\" theorem that's the harder part, but still doable.</p>",
        "id": 597532398,
        "sender_full_name": "Robert Hawkins",
        "timestamp": 1779714882
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>i am deep into yak-shaving territory, but <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39841\">#39841</a> is my best attempt at building the general version of the <code>HopfAlgebra.ofPrimitives</code> construction <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/31898\">#31898</a> needed.</p>",
